<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<mule xmlns:ee="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core" xmlns="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core"
	xmlns:doc="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/documentation"
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/core/current/mule.xsd
http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/ee/core/current/mule-ee.xsd">

	<!--
		Member matching, per the 2026-08-18 SDWC/Plative sync (Jacob Belizario,
		Niranja Nair) / this is the working spec, more specific than the
		general technical design on two points:

		1. Only two tiers. No name+DOB-only fallback with a confidence score.
		2. Tier 2 is a combination match on whichever of {Medicaid CIN, Last
		   Name, DOB} are actually populated on the incoming record, gated at
		   "at least two of the three fields present" / not "CIN and DOB
		   both required." Example confirmed on the call: CIN blank, Last
		   Name and DOB both present and exact -> still attempt the match.
		   CIN blank AND Last Name blank (DOB alone) -> do not attempt it.

		Never auto-creates a Person Account. No match at either tier means
		matchedMemberId stays null; the caller still creates the Assessment
		record, just with the Member lookup blank / confirmed on the call
		("you're not creating a person... keep the lookup blank").

		REVISED 2026-08-19 per the CIE Referral API || SF Field call with
		Toshiv Shrivastava: Tier 2's write-back (stamping the CIE Client ID
		onto the matched Account so Tier 1 catches it next run) is confirmed
		as real, intended design, not a speculative addition. It had been
		removed after the 2026-08-18 call since that call didn't mention it;
		Toshiv's 2026-08-19 walkthrough of the referral flow's matching logic
		describes the exact same mechanism ("if you find it, you update that
		client ID on the account record") as the shared basis both flows
		matching is built on.

		Caller contract:
			vars.matchRecord = {
				cieClientId: String | null,
				medicaidCin: String | null,
				lastName: String | null,
				dob: String | null   (YYYY-MM-DD, unquoted in SOQL as a Date literal)
			}

		Sets:
			vars.matchedMemberId   Salesforce Account Id, or null if no match
			vars.matchTier         1, 2, or 0 for no match

		Confirmed against the real sandbox via describe (2026-08-19):
		- Account.CIE_Client_ID__c exists and is flagged as an External ID
		  (Niranja added it after the second blocker was raised), used by
		  Tier 1. As of this writing no Account has it populated yet, so
		  Tier 1 will fall through to Tier 2 for all live test records.
		- The real field for Medicaid CIN on Account is Medi_Cal_ID__pc,
		  NOT Medi_Cal_CIN__pc as originally guessed from the data-mapping
		  workbook. LastName and PersonBirthdate are standard fields and
		  confirmed correct as written.
	-->
	<sub-flow name="member-matching-sub-flow" doc:id="7b3c4d5e-6f70-4a91-8b2c-3d4e5f607182">

		<logger level="INFO" doc:name="Before Member Matching" doc:id="8c4d5e6f-7081-4ba2-9c3d-4e5f60718293"
			message='#["Before Member Matching. cieClientId=" ++ (vars.matchRecord.cieClientId default "null")]' />

		<choice doc:name="Has CIE Client ID? (Tier 1)" doc:id="9d5e6f70-8192-4cb3-ad4e-5f6071829304">
			<when expression="#[vars.matchRecord.cieClientId != null]">
				<set-variable variableName="sfQuery" doc:name="Tier 1 Query" doc:id="ae6f7081-92a3-4dc4-be5f-607182930415"
					value="#[&quot;SELECT Id FROM Account WHERE CIE_Client_ID__c = '&quot; ++ vars.matchRecord.cieClientId ++ &quot;'&quot;]" />
				<flow-ref doc:name="Query Account (Tier 1)" doc:id="bf708192-a3b4-4ed5-cf60-718293041526" name="salesforce-query-operation-sub-flow" />
				<choice doc:name="Tier 1 Single Match?" doc:id="c0819203-b4c5-4fe6-d071-829304152637">
					<when expression="#[sizeOf(payload default []) == 1]">
						<set-variable variableName="matchedMemberId" doc:name="Set Matched Member (Tier 1)" doc:id="d1920314-c5d6-4f07-e182-930415263748"
							value="#[(payload default [])[0].Id]" />
						<set-variable variableName="matchTier" doc:name="Set Match Tier" doc:id="e2031425-d6e7-4018-f293-041526374859" value="1" />
					</when>
					<otherwise>
						<flow-ref doc:name="Try Tier 2" doc:id="04253647-f809-4230-1415-263748596071" name="member-matching-tier2-sub-flow" />
					</otherwise>
				</choice>
			</when>
			<otherwise>
				<flow-ref doc:name="Try Tier 2" doc:id="15364758-091a-4341-2526-374859607182" name="member-matching-tier2-sub-flow" />
			</otherwise>
		</choice>

		<logger level="INFO" doc:name="After Member Matching" doc:id="26475869-1a2b-4452-3637-485960718293"
			message='#[output application/json&#10;---&#10;{&#10;	message: "After Member Matching",&#10;	matchedMemberId: vars.matchedMemberId default null,&#10;	matchTier: vars.matchTier default 0&#10;}]' />

	</sub-flow>

	<!--
		Tier 2: combination match on whichever of {Medicaid CIN, Last Name,
		DOB} are populated, requiring at least two of the three. Builds the
		SOQL WHERE clause dynamically from only the populated fields, so a
		record missing CIN but carrying an exact Last Name + DOB still gets
		searched, per the call.

		BUG FOUND during full-flow testing (2026-08-19): CIE's Birthdate
		comes back as "1966-01-03Z", not a plain date. The trailing "Z"
		broke the SOQL date literal (MALFORMED_QUERY: unexpected token 'Z').
		Truncated to the first 10 characters (YYYY-MM-DD) before use.
	-->
	<sub-flow name="member-matching-tier2-sub-flow" doc:id="37586970-2b3c-4563-4748-596071829304">

		<set-variable variableName="tier2PopulatedFieldCount" doc:name="Count Populated Fields" doc:id="9a1b2c3d-4e5f-4061-7182-93a4b5c6d7e8"
			value="#[(if (vars.matchRecord.medicaidCin != null) 1 else 0)&#10;+ (if (vars.matchRecord.lastName != null) 1 else 0)&#10;+ (if (vars.matchRecord.dob != null) 1 else 0)]" />

		<choice doc:name="At Least Two Fields Populated?" doc:id="ab2c3d4e-5f60-4172-8293-a4b5c6d7e8f9">
			<when expression="#[vars.tier2PopulatedFieldCount &gt;= 2]">

				<ee:transform doc:name="Build Tier 2 Query" doc:id="bc3d4e5f-6071-4283-9304-b5c6d7e8f90a">
					<ee:message>
					</ee:message>
					<ee:variables>
						<ee:set-variable variableName="sfQuery"><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output text/plain
---
"SELECT Id FROM Account WHERE " ++
(
	[
		if (vars.matchRecord.medicaidCin != null) "Medi_Cal_ID__pc = '" ++ vars.matchRecord.medicaidCin ++ "'" else null,
		if (vars.matchRecord.lastName != null) "LastName = '" ++ vars.matchRecord.lastName ++ "'" else null,
		if (vars.matchRecord.dob != null) "PersonBirthdate = " ++ (vars.matchRecord.dob)[0 to 9] else null
	] filter ($ != null)
) joinBy " AND "]]></ee:set-variable>
					</ee:variables>
				</ee:transform>

				<flow-ref doc:name="Query Account (Tier 2)" doc:id="6a819203-5e6f-4896-a70a-718293041526" name="salesforce-query-operation-sub-flow" />
				<choice doc:name="Tier 2 Single Match?" doc:id="7b920314-6f70-49a7-b81b-829304152637">
					<when expression="#[sizeOf(payload default []) == 1]">
						<set-variable variableName="matchedMemberId" doc:name="Set Matched Member (Tier 2)" doc:id="8c031425-7081-4ab8-c92c-041526374859"
							value="#[(payload default [])[0].Id]" />
						<set-variable variableName="matchTier" doc:name="Set Match Tier" doc:id="9d142536-8192-4bc9-da3d-152637485960" value="2" />

						<!--
							Write-back, confirmed real on the 2026-08-19 call with
							Toshiv Shrivastava (see file header). Only fires when
							CIE actually sent a client id to write / current live
							test data has SDWC_Client_Id as null on every record,
							so this branch is coded but not yet exercised against
							a real value.
						-->
						<choice doc:name="Has CIE Client ID to Write Back?" doc:id="a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4708-8192-a3b4c5d6e7f8">
							<when expression="#[vars.matchRecord.cieClientId != null]">
								<set-variable variableName="sfObject" doc:name="Set sfObject for Write-Back" doc:id="b2c3d4e5-f607-4819-92a3-b4c5d6e7f809" value="Account" />
								<ee:transform doc:name="Write-Back Payload" doc:id="c3d4e5f6-0718-4a2b-a3b4-c5d6e7f8091a">
									<ee:message>
										<ee:set-payload><![CDATA[%dw 2.0
output application/java
---
{
	Id: vars.matchedMemberId,
	CIE_Client_ID__c: vars.matchRecord.cieClientId
}]]></ee:set-payload>
									</ee:message>
								</ee:transform>
								<flow-ref doc:name="Write Back CIE Client ID" doc:id="d4e5f607-1829-4b3c-b4c5-d6e7f8091a2b" name="salesforce-update-operation-sub-flow" />
							</when>
						</choice>
					</when>
					<otherwise>
						<set-variable variableName="matchedMemberId" doc:name="No Match at Tier 2" doc:id="e209132b-6687-4917-c98c-607182930415" value="#[null]" />
						<set-variable variableName="matchTier" doc:name="Set Match Tier" doc:id="f31a243c-7798-4a28-da9d-718293041526" value="0" />
					</otherwise>
				</choice>

			</when>
			<otherwise>
				<logger level="INFO" doc:name="Tier 2 Skipped: Insufficient Fields" doc:id="cd4e5f60-7182-4394-a415-c6d7e8f90a1b"
					message='#["Skipping Tier 2 match: fewer than two of {Medicaid CIN, Last Name, DOB} are populated."]' />
				<set-variable variableName="matchedMemberId" doc:name="No Match" doc:id="04253647-f809-4230-1415-263748596072" value="#[null]" />
				<set-variable variableName="matchTier" doc:name="Set Match Tier" doc:id="15364758-091a-4341-2526-374859607183" value="0" />
			</otherwise>
		</choice>

	</sub-flow>

</mule>
